msgid ""
"The same as ``response.body.decode(response.encoding)``, but the result is "
"cached after the first call, so you can access ``response.text`` multiple "
"times without extra overhead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/request-response.rst:1312
msgid ""
"``str(response.body)`` is not a correct way to convert the response body "
"into a string:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/request-response.rst:1315
msgid ""
">>> str(b\"body\")\n"
"\"b'body'\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/request-response.rst:1323
msgid ""
"A string with the encoding of this response. The encoding is resolved by "
"trying the following mechanisms, in order:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/request-response.rst:1326
msgid "the encoding passed in the ``__init__()`` method ``encoding`` argument"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/request-response.rst:1328
msgid ""
"the encoding of the `byte order mark`_ at the start of the response body"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/request-response.rst:1331
msgid ""
"the encoding declared in the Content-Type HTTP header. If this encoding is "
"not valid (i.e. unknown), it is ignored and the next resolution mechanism is "
"tried."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/request-response.rst:1335
msgid ""
"the encoding declared in the response body. The TextResponse class doesn't "
"provide any special functionality for this. However, the :class:"
"`HtmlResponse` and :class:`XmlResponse` classes do."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/request-response.rst:1339
msgid ""
"the encoding inferred by looking at the response body. This is the more "
"fragile method but also the last one tried."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/request-response.rst:1342
msgid ""
"This order matches the `encoding sniffing algorithm`_ of the HTML standard, "
"which web browsers follow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/request-response.rst:1345
msgid ""
"To resolve the encoding differently, determine it yourself and pass it "
"through :meth:`Response.replace` from a :ref:`downloader middleware <topics-"
"downloader-middleware>`. Give that middleware an order between those of :"
"class:`~scrapy.downloadermiddlewares.redirect.MetaRefreshMiddleware` (580) "
"and :class:`~scrapy.downloadermiddlewares.httpcompression."
"HttpCompressionMiddleware` (590), so that it gets a decompressed body and no "
"other component reads the response text before it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/request-response.rst:1355
msgid ""
"For example, to give a declaration in the response body precedence over the "
"Content-Type header:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/request-response.rst:1358
msgid ""
"from w3lib.encoding import html_body_declared_encoding, read_bom\n"
"\n"
"from scrapy.http import TextResponse\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"class BodyEncodingMiddleware:\n"
"    def process_response(self, request, response, spider):\n"
"        if not isinstance(response, TextResponse):\n"
"            return response\n"
"        if read_bom(response.body)[0]:\n"
"            return response\n"
"        encoding = html_body_declared_encoding(response.body)\n"
"        return response.replace(encoding=encoding) if encoding else response"
msgstr ""

